{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["כל נשיא בהם — the essential plain sense is thus: 'These twelve men you shall take' — from among those in Israel whose hearts moved them to go; you shall direct the people: who is the man who wishes to go to spy out the land? And from those who say they will go, you shall take and choose twelve from among them. And since brave men who are not fearful or fainthearted are fit to go through a foreign land and also to strengthen themselves and take fruit of the land, therefore it was necessary to make a proclamation, and the Holy One, blessed be He, did not designate them by name — as He did for the princes who counted Israel, and for the princes by whom He apportioned the land to Israel in אלה מסעי. For those were designated by name." "כל נשיא בהם — the reason that 'under' is בְּהֶם: its meaning is: each of these twelve shall be a prince among those volunteers who go — as in: 'כל שתה תחת רגליו'."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:50:08.447536994Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}